{"name":"Carnation","hex":"#fd798f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carnation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in King, Washington, United States.","An unincorporated community in Washington County, Oregon, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carnation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carnation (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Carnation is a brand of food products. The brand was especially known for its evaporated milk product created in 1899, then called Carnation Sterilized Cream and later called Carnation Evaporated Milk. The brand has since been used for other related products including milk-flavoring mixes, flavored beverages, flavor syrups, hot cocoa mixes, instant breakfasts, corn flakes, ice cream novelties, and dog food. Nestlé acquired the Carnation Company in 1985."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/20/Carnationlogo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnation_(brand)","wikidata":"Q2939676"},{"title":"Carnation (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Carnation\" , also known by its French title L'œillet, is a song by Japanese musician Ringo Sheena. It was released on November 2, 2011, two years after her previous solo single \"Ariamaru Tomi\" (2009), during a period where she primarily worked with her band Tokyo Jihen. The song was the eponymous theme song for the morning Asadora drama Carnation, starring Machiko Ono."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/SheenaCarnation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnation_(song)","wikidata":"Q11063552"},{"title":"Dianthus caryophyllus","blocks":[{"text":"Dianthus caryophyllus, commonly known as carnation or clove pink, is a species of Dianthus native to the Mediterranean region. While its exact natural range is uncertain due to extensive cultivation over the last 2,000 years, wild carnations are most common in the Mediterranean region. Carnations are prized for their wide variety of colors, delicate fringed petals, and fragrance, often described as spicy, clove-like, or reminiscent of a combination of cinnamon and nutmeg, hence the common name \"clove pink\". This aroma has made carnations a popular choice for use in perfumes, potpourri, and scented products. Culturally, carnations are associated with affection, distinction, and maternal love, with variations depending on color and area within its wide geographical range."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/W_carnation4051.jpg/330px-W_carnation4051.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianthus_caryophyllus","wikidata":"Q158984"},{"title":"Shades of pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink colors are usually light or desaturated shades of reds, roses, and magentas which are created on computer and television screens using the RGB color model and in printing with the CMYK color model. As such, it is an arbitrary classification of color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Color_icon_pink_v2.svg/330px-Color_icon_pink_v2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_pink","wikidata":"Q19847189"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Carnation_Milk_newspaper_ad.png/500px-Carnation_Milk_newspaper_ad.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Carnation_Milk_newspaper_ad.png/500px-Carnation_Milk_newspaper_ad.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Newspaper ad for Carnation Evaporated Milk, 1921","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarnation_Milk_newspaper_ad.png"},{"srcset":"htt